{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.QbetaPerBlockChiClosedForms","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.QbetaPerBlockChiClosedForms","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Pow","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Add","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Inv","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.unique","kind":"theorem","line":512,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L512-L550","doc":"**Theorem (uniqueness of `ZRecursionCoeffs` instances).** Any two\ninstances of `ZRecursionCoeffs` have the same coefficient sequence.\n\nThis is a structural consequence of the recursion: the initial values\n`a_0`, `a_1` plus the linear recursion determine every `a_n` uniquely.\nProof: strong induction on `n`; base cases discharged by `initial_0`\nand `initial_1`; step uses the recursion at `n = k+1` to solve for\n`a (k+2)` in terms of `a (k+1)` and `a k`, then applies IH.\n\n**Status**: sorry-free. Strong induction on `n`; base cases discharged\nby `initial_0`/`initial_1`; step solves the recursion at `n = k+1` for\n`a (k+2)` using the IH on `a (k+1)` and `a k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.recursion","kind":"theorem","line":509,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L509-L509","doc":"The 3-term recursion (proven from the q-difference equation\nfor `z`; sketched in the prearchimedean witness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.initial_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.initial_1","kind":"theorem","line":506,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L506-L506","doc":"`a_1 = 0` (the first derivative of `z(q)` at `q = 1` vanishes\nby symmetry under `q ↔ 1/q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.initial_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.initial_0","kind":"theorem","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L503-L503","doc":"`a_0 = 1/2` (from `z(1) = √1 / (1+1) = 1/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.a","kind":"def","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L501-L501","doc":"The Taylor coefficient sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs.mk","kind":"ctor","line":499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L499-L499","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZRecursionCoeffs","kind":"class","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L486-L510","doc":"**Class (3-term recursion for z(q) Taylor coefficients around q = 1).**\n\nThe Taylor coefficients `a_n` of `z(q) = √q / (1 + q)` expanded around\n`q = 1` satisfy the 3-term recursion\n  `4(n+1)·a_{n+1} + 6n·a_n + (2n−1)·a_{n−1} = 0`,  n ≥ 1,\nwith `a_0 = 1/2` and `a_1 = 0`. Source: the q-difference equation for\n`z(q)` (linear ODE with rational coefficients in q).\n\nFollowing §3b-cond, the recursion is axiomatised as a class so that\nthe (proven) extended z^k family recursions can consume it.\n\nSource: `qbeta_prearchimedean_z_recursion.witness.json` and\n`qbeta_c3_multiblock_recursion_attack.py` header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_vanish_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_vanish_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L463-L473","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3`).** The canonical\nΔτ_M vanishes at the classical point `q = 1`.\n\n**Proof**: each per-block `chi_block_λ` vanishes at `q = 1` (by\n`chi_blocks_vanish_at_one`), so the y_λ-weighted sum vanishes term-by-term\nregardless of the (finite) values of `y_λ(1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical","kind":"def","line":457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L457-L461","doc":"The canonical Δτ_M sum, conditional on a `CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3`\ninstance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.sum_dim_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.sum_dim_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L455-L455","doc":"Normalisation: weighted sum of dimensions equals 1.\n`dim V_(3) = 1, dim V_(2,1) = 2, dim V_(1,1,1) = 1` ⇒\n`y_(3) + 2·y_(2,1) + y_(1,1,1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.y111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.y111","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L451-L451","doc":"Canonical weight on the sign irrep `V_(1,1,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.y21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.y21","kind":"def","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L449-L449","doc":"Canonical weight on the 2-dim irrep `V_(2,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.y3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.y3","kind":"def","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L447-L447","doc":"Canonical weight on the trivial irrep `V_(3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.mk","kind":"ctor","line":445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L445-L445","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3","kind":"class","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L430-L455","doc":"**Class (canonical Wenzl–Markov weights for H_3(q)).**\n\nThis class axiomatises the canonical Wenzl–Markov weights `y_λ(q)`\nfor the n=3 Hecke algebra. Each field encodes a property the canonical\nweights satisfy. Following AGENTS.md §3b-cond, this class is the\nsingle point of conjectural input that downstream conditional\ntheorems (e.g. `delta_tau_M_canonical_vanish_at_one`) consume as\nan `[Instance]` hypothesis.\n\n**Conjectural status**: the existence of an instance that simultaneously\nsatisfies all four axioms below for the closed-form Wenzl–Markov\nweights is the open math. The closed forms involve `√q` via the\nMarkov parameter `z = markov_parameter q`. A concrete instance would\nencode them as `noncomputable def`s and verify each axiom; doing so\nrequires the Wenzl recursion's `√q` handling beyond `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markov_parameter_symmetric_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markov_parameter_symmetric_form","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L410-L428","doc":"**Theorem (symmetric form of the Markov parameter).** For `q > 0`,\n`z(q) = 1 / (√q + 1/√q)`.\n\nThis is the alternative defining form used in the canonical Wenzl\nconstruction. Proof outline: clear denominators on both sides,\nmultiply through by `(1 + q) · √q`, and use `Real.mul_self_sqrt :\n√q · √q = q` for `q ≥ 0` to identify the cross-terms.\n\n**Status**: sorry-free. Cross-multiply, use `Real.mul_self_sqrt :\n√q · √q = q` for `q ≥ 0`, finish with `field_simp; linarith`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markov_parameter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markov_parameter","kind":"def","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L393-L408","doc":"The Markov parameter `z(q) = √q / (1 + q)`. Pure archimedean\nconstruction — depends on `Real.sqrt`. Source: Wenzl.\n\n**Convention C, deliberately — not the canonical Markov parameter.** Owner\nruling R1 (2026-08-15) makes convention D, `z = q³/(q²+1)`, canonical and\nexcises C. This definition is kept **as the C-frame object** because every\nconsumer in this file (`delta_tau_M_canonical`, the `c_k` Taylor orders) is\nthe convention-C Q_β precision ladder, which bean `qou-cds1` blocks from\nmigration until the ladder is re-derived under D: `decayLadder_zC_threeRow_ne_zero`\n(`QOU.QBeta.MarkovZFullBarCondition`) makes the C-frame ladder and the mass\nchannel's three-row forcing mutually exclusive, so substituting `q³/(q²+1)` here\nwould not migrate the ladder, it would change what these declarations assert.\nEvery value derived from this definition is C-conditional; do not cite it as D.\nConvention D lives in `QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD` (`MarkovConventionSeparation.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_surrogate_hasDerivAt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_surrogate_hasDerivAt_one","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L268-L332","doc":"**Theorem (order-1 Taylor coefficient = −5/6).** The first derivative\nof `delta_tau_M_surrogate` at `q = 1` equals `−5/6`.\n\nPer the script's order-1 print: `Order 1:  -5/6`.\n\n**Status**: sorry-free. Standard quotient-rule derivative via\n`hasDerivAt_pow`, `HasDerivAt.add`, `HasDerivAt.sub`, `HasDerivAt.mul`,\n`HasDerivAt.div`, then `convert ... ; ring` + `norm_num` for the\nfinal numerical identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_surrogate_vanish_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_surrogate_vanish_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L259-L266","doc":"**Theorem (order-0 Taylor coefficient).** `delta_tau_M_surrogate 1 = 0`.\n\nThis is the classical-point vanishing — the y_λ-weighted sum\nof three per-block characters that each have a `(q^2-1)` factor\nmust vanish at `q = 1`. Per the script: `coeffs[0] = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_surrogate_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_surrogate_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L240-L255","doc":"**Theorem (surrogate Δτ_M closed form).** For all `q > 0`, the\ny_λ-surrogate-weighted sum of the per-block characters equals the\nrational closed form `delta_tau_M_surrogate q`. Pure ring identity\nafter clearing denominators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.one_plus_q_plus_q_sq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.one_plus_q_plus_q_sq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L235-L238","doc":"Helper: `1 + q + q² > 0` for any `q : ℝ` (sum of squares form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_surrogate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_surrogate","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L215-L233","doc":"Multi-block Δτ_M closed form under the rational-y_λ surrogate.\n\nSource (SymPy): `qbeta_c3_multiblock_recursion_attack.py` Step 1.\n\nNumerator: `2q¹⁷ − 2q¹⁶ − 5q¹⁵ + 4q¹⁴ + 8q¹³ − 9q¹² − 8q¹¹ + 9q¹⁰ + 11q⁹\n− 11q⁸ − 9q⁷ + 8q⁶ + 9q⁵ − 8q⁴ − 4q³ + 5q² + 2q − 2`\nDenominator: `4 q⁸ (q² + q + 1)`\n\nRestated 2026-09-07 for the canonical borromean `chi_block_21`; the grouped\nframe gave `(−q¹¹ + q¹⁰ − 2q⁹ + q⁸ + q⁶ − q⁵ − q³ + 2q² − q + 1)/(4q⁵(q²+q+1))`.\nBoth vanish at `q = 1` and agree on the order-1 and order-2 Taylor\ncoefficients.\n\nFor all `q > 0`, this equals `y_(3)·χ_(3) + y_(2,1)·χ_(2,1) + y_(1,1,1)·χ_(1,1,1)`\n(theorem `delta_tau_M_surrogate_eq_sum` below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.y_lambda_surrogate_111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.y_lambda_surrogate_111","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L211-L213","doc":"Per-block Wenzl–Markov weight surrogate `y_{(1,1,1)}(q) = 1 / ((1+q)(1+q+q²))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.y_lambda_surrogate_21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.y_lambda_surrogate_21","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L207-L209","doc":"Per-block Wenzl–Markov weight surrogate `y_{(2,1)}(q) = q / ((1+q)(1+q+q²))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.y_lambda_surrogate_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.y_lambda_surrogate_3","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L196-L205","doc":"Per-block Wenzl–Markov weight surrogate `y_{(3)}(q) = q² / ((1+q)(1+q+q²))`.\n\nNOT canonical — the canonical weight involves `√q` (via the Markov\nparameter `z = √q / (1+q)`). The surrogate is retained because it\npreserves the per-block dimension structure `{q², q, 1} / ((1+q)(1+q+q²))`\nand is sufficient to expose the NEAR-MATCH cross-anchor diagnostic.\nThe CANONICAL version is axiomatised in §Extension #4 below.\nSource: `qbeta_c3_multiblock_recursion_attack.py::y_lambda_h3_symbolic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_blocks_have_q2_minus_1_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_blocks_have_q2_minus_1_factor","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L136-L172","doc":"**Theorem (q²−1 factor in all three blocks).** Every per-block\ncharacter $\\chi_\\lambda(\\Delta_{T_\\beta})$ factors as $(q^2 - 1)$\ntimes a rational function of $q$ on the physical regime $q > 0$\n(so the classical limit $q \\to 1^+$ is the structural source of\nthe vanishing — see `chi_blocks_vanish_at_one`).\n\nThe identity $q^2 - 1 = (q-1)(q+1)$ would algebraically extend the\nvanishing to $q = -1$ as well, but this theorem is stated under\n$q > 0$ to match the physical regime of $\\chi_\\lambda$ (where the\n$1/q^k$ denominators in the closed forms are well-defined and\npositive); the $q = -1$ root is outside scope.\n\nThis is the structural source of the order-$w$ leading term in the\nTaylor expansion around $q = 1$: $q^2 - 1 = 2w + w^2$ where\n$w = q - 1$. Each block contributes at first order in $w$, with\nthe per-block ε¹-order coefficients $\\{-2, -1, -2\\}$ from the\nwitness's `taylor_coefficients_per_block_ε_order` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_block_antipode_pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_block_antipode_pairing","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L117-L134","doc":"**Theorem (antipode pairing).** Under the substitution $q \\mapsto 1/q$\nthe trivial-irrep character $\\chi_{(3)}$ maps to the sign-irrep\ncharacter $\\chi_{(1,1,1)}$:\n\n  $\\chi_{(1,1,1)}(q) = q^{-4} \\cdot \\chi_{(3)}(q)$.\n\nThis reflects the standard Hecke-algebra identity\n$V_{(3)} \\otimes V_{\\text{sign}} = V_{(1,1,1)}$, with the $q^{-4}$\nprefactor coming from the framing weight (degree-$4$ shift between\nthe $q^{-1}$- and $q^{-5}$-denominators).\n\nProof: direct rational arithmetic; clear denominators and apply\n`ring`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms","label":"prop:qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_blocks_vanish_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_blocks_vanish_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L105-L115","doc":"**Theorem (vanishing at $q = 1$).** Each per-block character\n$\\chi_\\lambda(\\Delta_{T_\\beta})$ vanishes at the classical point $q = 1$.\n\nThis confirms $\\Delta\\tau_M(1) = 0$ regardless of the y_λ weights —\nthe classical limit is trivial for every block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_block_111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_block_111","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L94-L103","doc":"Per-block character $\\chi_{(1,1,1)}(\\Delta_{T_\\beta})(q)$ on the\nsign irrep $V_{(1,1,1)}$.\n\nClosed form: $-(q^2 - 1)(q^2 + 1)^2 / (4q^5)$.\n\nAntipode pair with `chi_block_3`: $\\chi_{(1,1,1)}(q) = q^{-4} \\cdot \\chi_{(3)}(q)$,\nformalised below as `q⁻¹ ^ 4 * chi_block_3 q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_block_21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_block_21","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L74-L92","doc":"Per-block character $\\chi_{(2,1)}(\\Delta_{T_\\beta})(q)$ on the\n2-dim irrep $V_{(2,1)}$.\n\nClosed form: $(q^2 - 1)(q^4 + 1)P(q) / (4q^{9})$ with\n$P(q) = 2q^{12} - 5q^{10} + 5q^{8} - 5q^{6} + 5q^{4} - 5q^{2} + 2$.\n\n**The only ordering-dependent block, and the only 2-dimensional one.**\nIn $V_{(3)}$ and $V_{(1,1,1)}$ the generators act by scalars and commute, so\nthe intra-nucleon braid ordering cannot reach those characters. Here it can.\nThe form above is the canonical borromean word $(\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1})^3$\n(beans `qou-hu1f` / `qou-eddc`); the superseded grouped word gave\n$(q^2-1)(-q^4-1)/(4q^3)$, which was linear in $h = q - 1/q$ up to the $h^3$\nterm. The canonical form is degree 9 in $h$, still odd, still with the same\n$-h/2$ leading term — which is why $P(1) = -1$ and the two frames agree at\nthe classical point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_block_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_block_3","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-per-block-chi-closed-forms.lean#L65-L72","doc":"Per-block character $\\chi_{(3)}(\\Delta_{T_\\beta})(q)$ on the trivial\nirrep $V_{(3)}$.\n\nClosed form: $-(q^2 - 1)(q^2 + 1)^2 / (4q)$.\nSource: `qbeta-per-block-paper-closed-forms.witness.json`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}